        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(matrix): handle stdout/stderr stream errors in dependency commands",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add stdout/stderr `error` handlers to Matrix dependency bootstrap commands\n- reuse the existing finalize path with a failed command result and terminate the child process on stream failure\n- cover stdout and stderr stream errors with a focused regression test\n- collision check: no open PR found for the Matrix dependency command stream-error issue or `extensions/matrix/src/matrix/deps.ts`; the only fuzzy search hit was an unrelated Telegram PR\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.extension-matrix.config.ts extensions/matrix/src/matrix/deps.test.ts -t \"runFixedCommandWithTimeout\"` — passed; 1 file, 2 tests passed, 8 skipped\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior addressed: Matrix dependency bootstrap commands collected child stdout/stderr `data` but did not handle readable stream `error`, so a stream `EPIPE` could bypass the command result handling.\nReal environment tested: mocked dependency command child processes using Node `PassThrough` streams in Vitest; no real Matrix SDK download was required.\nExact steps or command run after this patch: emitted `error` on mocked stdout and stderr streams while `runFixedCommandWithTimeout` was awaiting command completion.\nEvidence after fix: each emitted stream error did not throw out of band, killed the child process with `SIGTERM`, and resolved to `{ code: 1, stdout: \"\", stderr: \"stdout stream failed: EPIPE\" }` or the stderr equivalent.\nObserved result after fix: dependency command stream failures now return a bounded command failure result instead of becoming unhandled stream errors.\nWhat was not tested: full CI and a live Matrix crypto runtime bootstrap download.",
